  "name": "Modeling Walleye Pollock Recruitment in the Eastern Bering Sea: Use of Physical Data Integrated with Stock Assessment Information",
  "description": "The assessment of Eastern Bering Sea (EBS) Walleye Pollock presented to managers has increasingly been sensitive to year-class abundance estimates prior to their availability to the fishery. The fishery from this region has annually produced an excess of 1 million tons of Pollock for the past two decades. Data from two surveys proved to be crucial in developing a harvest strategy for 1997 and for projecting the expected fishery impacts in the short term (for 1998 - 2000).\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: To show a model of the Walleye Pollock recruitment in the eastern Bering Sea: use of physical data integrated with stock assessment information",
  "url": "https://zenodo.org/records/23506480",
